{"id":"mahabharata-1-060","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":60,"title":"षष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 60 · The lineages of the gods and sages","summary":{"en":"The genealogy continues with the eleven Rudras, the twelve Adityas with Vishnu the youngest, the Vasus, the descendants of the great sages, Dharma's sons, and the origin of birds, beasts and other creatures. Hearing it is said to purify a man of sin.","kn":"ಹನ್ನೊಂದು ರುದ್ರರು, ಕಿರಿಯನಾದ ವಿಷ್ಣುವಿನೊಂದಿಗೆ ಹನ್ನೆರಡು ಆದಿತ್ಯರು, ವಸುಗಳು, ಮಹರ್ಷಿಗಳ ಸಂತತಿ, ಧರ್ಮನ ಪುತ್ರರು ಮತ್ತು ಪಕ್ಷಿ ಮೃಗಾದಿಗಳ ಉತ್ಪತ್ತಿಯೊಂದಿಗೆ ವಂಶಾವಳಿ ಮುಂದುವರಿಯುತ್ತದೆ. ಇದನ್ನು ಕೇಳುವುದರಿಂದ ಪಾಪ ಪರಿಹಾರವಾಗುತ್ತದೆಂದು ಹೇಳಲಾಗಿದೆ.","hi":"वंशावली ग्यारह रुद्रों, सबसे छोटे विष्णु सहित बारह आदित्यों, वसुओं, महर्षियों की सन्तति, धर्म के पुत्रों और पक्षियों, पशुओं आदि की उत्पत्ति के साथ आगे बढ़ती है। कहा गया है कि इसे सुनने से मनुष्य पापमुक्त होता है।","te":"పదకొండు మంది రుద్రులు, చిన్నవాడైన విష్ణువుతో పన్నెండు మంది ఆదిత్యులు, వసువులు, మహర్షుల సంతతి, ధర్ముని కుమారులు, పక్షులు మృగాలు మొదలైన వాటి ఉత్పత్తితో వంశావళి కొనసాగుతుంది. దీనిని వినడం వల్ల పాపాలు తొలగుతాయని చెప్పబడింది.","ta":"பதினொரு ருத்ரர்கள், இளையவரான விஷ்ணுவுடன் பன்னிரண்டு ஆதித்யர்கள், வஸுக்கள், மகரிஷிகளின் சந்ததி, தர்மனின் புதல்வர்கள், பறவைகள் விலங்குகள் முதலியவற்றின் தோற்றம் என வம்சாவளி தொடர்கிறது. இதைக் கேட்பவன் பாவம் நீங்கித் தூய்மை அடைவான் என்று சொல்லப்படுகிறது.","ml":"പതിനൊന്ന് രുദ്രന്മാർ, വിഷ്ണു ഇളയവനായ പന്ത്രണ്ട് ആദിത്യന്മാർ, വസുക്കൾ, മഹർഷിമാരുടെ സന്തതികൾ, ധർമ്മത്തിന്റെ പുത്രന്മാർ, പക്ഷികളുടെയും മൃഗങ്ങളുടെയും മറ്റു ജീവികളുടെയും ഉത്പത്തി എന്നിവയോടെ വംശാവലി തുടരുന്നു. ഇത് കേൾക്കുന്നത് മനുഷ്യനെ പാപത്തിൽനിന്ന് ശുദ്ധീകരിക്കുമെന്ന് പറയപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.60; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"अंशावतरणपर्व","titleEn":"Amshavatarana Parva (Partial incarnations)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ब्रह्मणो मानसाः पुत्रा विदिताः षण्महर्षयः ।\nएकादश सुताः स्थाणोः ख्याताः परममानसाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahma's mind-born sons are known as the six great sages; and Sthanu is famed to have eleven sons of supreme mind."}},{"n":2,"text":"मृगव्याधश्च शर्वश्च निरृतिश्च महायशाः ।\nअजैकपादहिर्बुध्न्यः पिनाकी च परंतपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are Mrigavyadha, Sharva, and the greatly famed Nirriti; Ajaikapada, Ahirbudhnya, and Pinaki, tormentor of foes;"}},{"n":3,"text":"दहनोऽथेश्वरश्चैव कपाली च महाद्युतिः ।\nस्थाणुर्भवश्च भगवान्रुद्रा एकादश स्मृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dahana, Ishvara, and Kapali of great splendor; Sthanu and the lord Bhava: these are remembered as the eleven Rudras."}},{"n":4,"text":"मरीचिरङ्गिरा अत्रिः पुलस्त्यः पुलहः क्रतुः ।\nषडेते ब्रह्मणः पुत्रा वीर्यवन्तो महर्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Marichi, Angiras, Atri, Pulastya, Pulaha and Kratu: these six are the mighty great-sage sons of Brahma."}},{"n":5,"text":"त्रयस्त्वङ्गिरसः पुत्रा लोके सर्वत्र विश्रुताः ।\nबृहस्पतिरुतथ्यश्च संवर्तश्च धृतव्रताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Angiras had three sons, famed everywhere in the world: Brihaspati, Utathya and Samvarta, firm in their vows."}},{"n":6,"text":"अत्रेस्तु बहवः पुत्राः श्रूयन्ते मनुजाधिप ।\nसर्वे वेदविदः सिद्धाः शान्तात्मानो महर्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Atri is heard to have many sons, lord of men, all knowers of the Veda, accomplished, tranquil-minded great sages."}},{"n":7,"text":"राक्षसास्तु पुलस्त्यस्य वानराः किंनरास्तथा ।\nपुलहस्य मृगाः सिंहा व्याघ्राः किंपुरुषास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pulastya's offspring were rakshasas, monkeys and kinnaras; Pulaha's were deer, lions, tigers and kimpurushas."}},{"n":8,"text":"क्रतोः क्रतुसमाः पुत्राः पतंगसहचारिणः ।\nविश्रुतास्त्रिषु लोकेषु सत्यव्रतपरायणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kratu's sons were equal to Kratu, companions of the sun's rays, famed in the three worlds and devoted to truth."}},{"n":9,"text":"दक्षस्त्वजायताङ्गुष्ठाद्दक्षिणाद्भगवानृषिः ।\nब्रह्मणः पृथिवीपाल पुत्रः पुत्रवतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Daksha was born from Brahma's right thumb, the holy sage, son of Brahma, best of those who have sons, protector of the earth."}},{"n":10,"text":"वामादजायताङ्गुष्ठाद्भार्या तस्य महात्मनः ।\nतस्यां पञ्चाशतं कन्याः स एवाजनयन्मुनिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From his left thumb was born the wife of that great soul, and by her the sage fathered fifty daughters."}},{"n":11,"text":"ताः सर्वास्त्वनवद्याङ्ग्यः कन्याः कमललोचनाः ।\nपुत्रिकाः स्थापयामास नष्टपुत्रः प्रजापतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All those faultless-limbed, lotus-eyed girls the Prajapati, who had lost his sons, appointed as daughters who would stand in the place of sons."}},{"n":12,"text":"ददौ स दश धर्माय सप्तविंशतिमिन्दवे ।\nदिव्येन विधिना राजन्कश्यपाय त्रयोदश ॥","meaning":{"en":"He gave ten to Dharma, twenty-seven to the Moon, and thirteen to Kashyapa, by the divine rite, king."}},{"n":13,"text":"नामतो धर्मपत्न्यस्ताः कीर्त्यमाना निबोध मे ।\nकीर्तिर्लक्ष्मीर्धृतिर्मेधा पुष्टिः श्रद्धा क्रिया तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear from me the names of Dharma's wives as I recite them: Kirti, Lakshmi, Dhriti, Medha, Pushti, Shraddha, Kriya,"}},{"n":14,"text":"बुद्धिर्लज्जा मतिश्चैव पत्न्यो धर्मस्य ता दश ।\nद्वाराण्येतानि धर्मस्य विहितानि स्वयंभुवा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Buddhi, Lajja and Mati: these ten are the wives of Dharma. These are the gates of Dharma, established by the Self-born."}},{"n":15,"text":"सप्तविंशति सोमस्य पत्न्यो लोके परिश्रुताः ।\nकालस्य नयने युक्ताः सोमपत्न्यः शुभव्रताः ।\nसर्वा नक्षत्रयोगिन्यो लोकयात्राविधौ स्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The twenty-seven wives of Soma are renowned in the world; those of good vows, the Moon's wives, are engaged in leading time, and all are joined with the lunar mansions, set in the working of the world."}},{"n":16,"text":"पितामहो मुनिर्देवस्तस्य पुत्रः प्रजापतिः ।\nतस्याष्टौ वसवः पुत्रास्तेषां वक्ष्यामि विस्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The grandfather, the sage and god, had a son, the Prajapati; his eight sons were the Vasus, of whom I will speak in detail."}},{"n":17,"text":"धरो ध्रुवश्च सोमश्च अहश्चैवानिलोऽनलः ।\nप्रत्यूषश्च प्रभासश्च वसवोऽष्टाविति स्मृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhara, Dhruva, Soma, Aha, Anila, Anala, Pratyusha and Prabhasa are remembered as the eight Vasus."}},{"n":18,"text":"धूम्रायाश्च धरः पुत्रो ब्रह्मविद्यो ध्रुवस्तथा ।\nचन्द्रमास्तु मनस्विन्याः श्वसायाः श्वसनस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhara was the son of Dhumra, and Dhruva was the knower of Brahman; the Moon was the son of Manasvini, and Shvasana of Shvasa."}},{"n":19,"text":"रतायाश्चाप्यहः पुत्रः शाण्डिल्याश्च हुताशनः ।\nप्रत्यूषश्च प्रभासश्च प्रभातायाः सुतौ स्मृतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Aha was the son of Rata, and Hutashana of Shandilya; Pratyusha and Prabhasa are remembered as the two sons of Prabhata."}},{"n":20,"text":"धरस्य पुत्रो द्रविणो हुतहव्यवहस्तथा ।\nध्रुवस्य पुत्रो भगवान्कालो लोकप्रकालनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhara's sons were Dravina and Hutahavyavaha; Dhruva's son was the lord Kala, who drives the worlds."}},{"n":21,"text":"सोमस्य तु सुतो वर्चा वर्चस्वी येन जायते ।\nमनोहरायाः शिशिरः प्राणोऽथ रमणस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Soma's son was Varcha, through whom radiance is born; Manohara's sons were Shishira, Prana and Ramana."}},{"n":22,"text":"अह्नः सुतः स्मृतो ज्योतिः श्रमः शान्तस्तथा मुनिः ।\nअग्नेः पुत्रः कुमारस्तु श्रीमाञ्शरवणालयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Aha's sons are remembered as Jyotis, Shrama, Shanta and Muni; Agni's son was Kumara, the glorious one who dwells in the reed thicket."}},{"n":23,"text":"तस्य शाखो विशाखश्च नैगमेशश्च पृष्ठजः ।\nकृत्तिकाभ्युपपत्तेश्च कार्त्तिकेय इति स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His followers were Shakha, Vishakha and Naigamesha, who was born after; because the Krittikas took him up, he is remembered as Karttikeya."}},{"n":24,"text":"अनिलस्य शिवा भार्या तस्याः पुत्रः पुरोजवः ।\nअविज्ञातगतिश्चैव द्वौ पुत्रावनिलस्य तु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Anila's wife was Shiva; her son was Purojava, and Avijnatagati too: Anila's two sons."}},{"n":25,"text":"प्रत्यूषस्य विदुः पुत्रमृषिं नाम्नाथ देवलम् ।\nद्वौ पुत्रौ देवलस्यापि क्षमावन्तौ मनीषिणौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pratyusha's son is known to be the sage named Devala; Devala too had two sons, patient and wise."}},{"n":26,"text":"बृहस्पतेस्तु भगिनी वरस्त्री ब्रह्मचारिणी ।\nयोगसिद्धा जगत्सर्वमसक्तं विचरत्युत ।\nप्रभासस्य तु भार्या सा वसूनामष्टमस्य ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brihaspati's sister was an excellent woman, a celibate, perfect in yoga, who roams the whole world unattached; she was the wife of Prabhasa, the eighth of the Vasus."}},{"n":27,"text":"विश्वकर्मा महाभागो जज्ञे शिल्पप्रजापतिः ।\nकर्ता शिल्पसहस्राणां त्रिदशानां च वर्धकिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fortunate Vishvakarma was born, the Prajapati of crafts, maker of thousands of crafts and builder for the gods."}},{"n":28,"text":"भूषणानां च सर्वेषां कर्ता शिल्पवतां वरः ।\nयो दिव्यानि विमानानि देवतानां चकार ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is the maker of all ornaments, best of artisans, who made the divine aerial cars of the gods."}},{"n":29,"text":"मनुष्याश्चोपजीवन्ति यस्य शिल्पं महात्मनः ।\nपूजयन्ति च यं नित्यं विश्वकर्माणमव्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Humans live by the craft of that great soul, and always worship him, Vishvakarma, the imperishable."}},{"n":30,"text":"स्तनं तु दक्षिणं भित्त्वा ब्रह्मणो नरविग्रहः ।\nनिःसृतो भगवान्धर्मः सर्वलोकसुखावहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Splitting Brahma's right breast, the lord Dharma came out in human form, bringer of happiness to all the worlds."}},{"n":31,"text":"त्रयस्तस्य वराः पुत्राः सर्वभूतमनोहराः ।\nशमः कामश्च हर्षश्च तेजसा लोकधारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He had three excellent sons, charming to all beings: Shama, Kama and Harsha, who sustain the worlds with their energy."}},{"n":32,"text":"कामस्य तु रतिर्भार्या शमस्य प्राप्तिरङ्गना ।\nनन्दी तु भार्या हर्षस्य यत्र लोकाः प्रतिष्ठिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kama's wife was Rati, Shama's wife was Prapti, and Harsha's wife was Nandi, in whom the worlds rest."}},{"n":33,"text":"मरीचेः कश्यपः पुत्रः कश्यपस्य सुरासुराः ।\nजज्ञिरे नृपशार्दूल लोकानां प्रभवस्तु सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Marichi's son was Kashyapa, and from Kashyapa the gods and asuras were born, tiger among kings; he is the source of the worlds."}},{"n":34,"text":"त्वाष्ट्री तु सवितुर्भार्या वडवारूपधारिणी ।\nअसूयत महाभागा सान्तरिक्षेऽश्विनावुभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tvashtri's daughter, Savita's wife, who took the form of a mare, the fortunate one, bore both Ashvins in the sky."}},{"n":35,"text":"द्वादशैवादितेः पुत्राः शक्रमुख्या नराधिप ।\nतेषामवरजो विष्णुर्यत्र लोकाः प्रतिष्ठिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Aditi had twelve sons, led by Shakra, lord of men; the youngest of them is Vishnu, in whom the worlds rest."}},{"n":36,"text":"त्रयस्त्रिंशत इत्येते देवास्तेषामहं तव ।\nअन्वयं संप्रवक्ष्यामि पक्षैश्च कुलतो गणान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These are the thirty-three gods. I will tell you their descent, and the groups by their wings and families."}},{"n":37,"text":"रुद्राणामपरः पक्षः साध्यानां मरुतां तथा ।\nवसूनां भार्गवं विद्याद्विश्वेदेवांस्तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is another wing of the Rudras, and of the Sadhyas and the Maruts; know the Bhargava as among the Vasus, and likewise the Vishvedevas."}},{"n":38,"text":"वैनतेयस्तु गरुडो बलवानरुणस्तथा ।\nबृहस्पतिश्च भगवानादित्येष्वेव गण्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Garuda, the mighty son of Vinata, and Aruna, and the lord Brihaspati, are counted among the Adityas."}},{"n":39,"text":"अश्विभ्यां गुह्यकान्विद्धि सर्वौषध्यस्तथा पशून् ।\nएष देवगणो राजन्कीर्तितस्तेऽनुपूर्वशः ।\nयं कीर्तयित्वा मनुजः सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know the guhyakas, all the herbs and animals as belonging to the two Ashvins. This is the host of gods, told to you in order, king; one who recites it is freed from all sins."}},{"n":40,"text":"ब्रह्मणो हृदयं भित्त्वा निःसृतो भगवान्भृगुः ।\nभृगोः पुत्रः कविर्विद्वाञ्शुक्रः कविसुतो ग्रहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lord Bhrigu came out, splitting Brahma's heart. Bhrigu's son was the wise Kavi; Kavi's son was Shukra, the planet."}},{"n":41,"text":"त्रैलोक्यप्राणयात्रार्थे वर्षावर्षे भयाभये ।\nस्वयंभुवा नियुक्तः सन्भुवनं परिधावति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Appointed by the Self-born for the sustenance of the three worlds, for rain and drought, fear and safety, he travels around the world."}},{"n":42,"text":"योगाचार्यो महाबुद्धिर्दैत्यानामभवद्गुरुः ।\nसुराणां चापि मेधावी ब्रह्मचारी यतव्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A teacher of yoga, of great intellect, he became the preceptor of the Daityas, and also of the gods, wise, celibate, of firm vows."}},{"n":43,"text":"तस्मिन्नियुक्ते विभुना योगक्षेमाय भार्गवे ।\nअन्यमुत्पादयामास पुत्रं भृगुरनिन्दितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Bhargava was appointed by the lord to secure the welfare of the worlds, Bhrigu fathered another blameless son."}},{"n":44,"text":"च्यवनं दीप्ततपसं धर्मात्मानं मनीषिणम् ।\nयः स रोषाच्च्युतो गर्भान्मातुर्मोक्षाय भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"This was Chyavana, of blazing austerity, righteous and wise, who fell from the womb in anger to free his mother, Bharata."}},{"n":45,"text":"आरुषी तु मनोः कन्या तस्य पत्नी मनीषिणः ।\nऔर्वस्तस्यां समभवदूरुं भित्त्वा महायशाः ।\nमहातपा महातेजा बाल एव गुणैर्युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Aruchi was the daughter of Manu and the wife of that wise man; Aurva, greatly famed, was born of her, bursting her thigh, great in austerity, of great splendor, endowed with merits even as a child."}},{"n":46,"text":"ऋचीकस्तस्य पुत्रस्तु जमदग्निस्ततोऽभवत् ।\nजमदग्नेस्तु चत्वार आसन्पुत्रा महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His son was Richika, and from him Jamadagni was born. The great-souled Jamadagni had four sons."}},{"n":47,"text":"रामस्तेषां जघन्योऽभूदजघन्यैर्गुणैर्युतः ।\nसर्वशस्त्रास्त्रकुशलः क्षत्रियान्तकरो वशी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama was the youngest of them, but not youngest in qualities, skilled in all weapons and missiles, self-controlled, the ender of the kshatriyas."}},{"n":48,"text":"और्वस्यासीत्पुत्रशतं जमदग्निपुरोगमम् ।\nतेषां पुत्रसहस्राणि बभूवुर्भृगुविस्तरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Aurva had a hundred sons, headed by Jamadagni; they had thousands of sons, the spread of the Bhrigus."}},{"n":49,"text":"द्वौ पुत्रौ ब्रह्मणस्त्वन्यौ ययोस्तिष्ठति लक्षणम् ।\nलोके धाता विधाता च यौ स्थितौ मनुना सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahma had two other sons in whom his mark remains: Dhatri and Vidhatri, who stay in the world with Manu."}},{"n":50,"text":"तयोरेव स्वसा देवी लक्ष्मीः पद्मगृहा शुभा ।\nतस्यास्तु मानसाः पुत्रास्तुरगा व्योमचारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their sister was the goddess Lakshmi, fair, who lives in a lotus; her mind-born sons were horses that move through the sky."}},{"n":51,"text":"वरुणस्य भार्या ज्येष्ठा तु शुक्राद्देवी व्यजायत ।\nतस्याः पुत्रं बलं विद्धि सुरां च सुरनन्दिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The eldest wife of Varuna, a goddess, was born of Shukra; know her son as Bala, and her daughter as Sura, delight of the gods."}},{"n":52,"text":"प्रजानामन्नकामानामन्योन्यपरिभक्षणात् ।\nअधर्मस्तत्र संजातः सर्वभूतविनाशनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From creatures eating one another in desire for food, Adharma arose, the destroyer of all beings."}},{"n":53,"text":"तस्यापि निरृतिर्भार्या नैरृता येन राक्षसाः ।\nघोरास्तस्यास्त्रयः पुत्राः पापकर्मरताः सदा ।\nभयो महाभयश्चैव मृत्युर्भूतान्तकस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"His wife was Nirriti, from whom the rakshasas are called Nairritas. She had three fearsome sons, always fond of evil deeds: Bhaya, Mahabhaya and Mrityu, the ender of beings."}},{"n":54,"text":"काकीं श्येनीं च भासीं च धृतराष्ट्रीं तथा शुकीम् ।\nताम्रा तु सुषुवे देवी पञ्चैता लोकविश्रुताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The goddess Tamra bore Kaki, Shyeni, Bhasi, Dhritarashtri and Shuki: these five are famed in the world."}},{"n":55,"text":"उलूकान्सुषुवे काकी श्येनी श्येनान्व्यजायत ।\nभासी भासानजनयद्गृध्रांश्चैव जनाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kaki bore owls, Shyeni bore hawks, Bhasi bore Bhasa birds and vultures, lord of men."}},{"n":56,"text":"धृतराष्ट्री तु हंसांश्च कलहंसांश्च सर्वशः ।\nचक्रवाकांश्च भद्रं ते प्रजज्ञे सा तु भामिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtri bore geese, and ruddy geese of every kind, and chakravaka birds; good fortune to you."}},{"n":57,"text":"शुकी विजज्ञे धर्मज्ञ शुकानेव मनस्विनी ।\nकल्याणगुणसंपन्ना सर्वलक्षणपूजिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shuki, knower of dharma, strong-minded, endowed with fine qualities and honored for all her marks, bore parrots only."}},{"n":58,"text":"नव क्रोधवशा नारीः प्रजज्ञेऽप्यात्मसंभवाः ।\nमृगीं च मृगमन्दां च हरिं भद्रमनामपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krodhavasha bore nine daughters, born of herself: Mrigi, Mrigamanda, Hari, Bhadramana,"}},{"n":59,"text":"मातङ्गीमथ शार्दूलीं श्वेतां सुरभिमेव च ।\nसर्वलक्षणसंपन्नां सुरसां च यशस्विनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Matangi, Shardula, Shveta, Surabhi, and Surasa, famed and endowed with all marks."}},{"n":60,"text":"अपत्यं तु मृगाः सर्वे मृग्या नरवरात्मज ।\nऋक्षाश्च मृगमन्दायाः सृमराश्चमरा अपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"All deer are the offspring of Mrigi, son of the best of men; bears, srimaras and yaks are of Mrigamanda."}},{"n":61,"text":"ततस्त्वैरावतं नागं जज्ञे भद्रमना सुतम् ।\nऐरावतः सुतस्तस्या देवनागो महागजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhadramana bore as her son the elephant Airavata, a divine elephant, a great one."}},{"n":62,"text":"हर्याश्च हरयोऽपत्यं वानराश्च तरस्विनः ।\nगोलाङ्गूलांश्च भद्रं ते हर्याः पुत्रान्प्रचक्षते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hari's offspring were the Haris, and swift monkeys, and langurs; Hari's sons are called the long-tailed ones, good fortune to you."}},{"n":63,"text":"प्रजज्ञे त्वथ शार्दूली सिंहान्व्याघ्रांश्च भारत ।\nद्वीपिनश्च महाभाग सर्वानेव न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shardula bore lions and tigers, Bharata, and leopards, great one, no doubt all of them."}},{"n":64,"text":"मातङ्ग्यास्त्वथ मातङ्गा अपत्यानि नराधिप ।\nदिशागजं तु श्वेताख्यं श्वेताजनयदाशुगम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Matangi's offspring were elephants, lord of men; Shveta bore the swift elephant of the quarter named Shveta."}},{"n":65,"text":"तथा दुहितरौ राजन्सुरभिर्वै व्यजायत ।\nरोहिणीं चैव भद्रं ते गन्धर्वीं च यशस्विनीम् ।\nरोहिण्यां जज्ञिरे गावो गन्धर्व्यां वाजिनः सुताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surabhi bore two daughters, king: Rohini, and the famed Gandharvi, good fortune to you. From Rohini cows were born, and from Gandharvi horses."}},{"n":66,"text":"सुरसाजनयन्नागान्राजन्कद्रूश्च पन्नगान् ।\nसप्त पिण्डफलान्वृक्षाननलापि व्यजायत ।\nअनलायाः शुकी पुत्री कद्र्वास्तु सुरसा सुता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surasa bore nagas, and Kadru bore serpents; Anala bore the seven trees with fruits in clusters. Anala's daughter was Shuki, and Kadru's daughter was Surasa."}},{"n":67,"text":"अरुणस्य भार्या श्येनी तु वीर्यवन्तौ महाबलौ ।\nसंपातिं जनयामास तथैव च जटायुषम् ।\nद्वौ पुत्रौ विनतायास्तु विख्यातौ गरुडारुणौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Aruna's wife Shyeni bore two mighty, powerful sons: Sampati and Jatayu; Vinata's two sons are famed as Garuda and Aruna."}},{"n":68,"text":"इत्येष सर्वभूतानां महतां मनुजाधिप ।\nप्रभवः कीर्तितः सम्यङ्मया मतिमतां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"So I have rightly told you the origin of all the great beings, best of the wise, lord of men."}},{"n":69,"text":"यं श्रुत्वा पुरुषः सम्यक्पूतो भवति पाप्मनः ।\nसर्वज्ञतां च लभते गतिमग्र्यां च विन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who hears it is properly purified of sin, gains omniscience, and attains the highest state."}}]}]}